<section id="part-3-the-merging-process" class="level4">
<h4 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="part-3-the-merging-process">Part 3: The Merging Process</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Lines 10–11:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?i%20=%201"> and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?j%20=%201">
<ul>
<li><strong>Meaning:</strong> We set our “pointers”. <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?i"> points to the top card of the Left pile (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L%5B1%5D%20=%204">). <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?j"> points to the top card of the Right pile (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?R%5B1%5D%20=%202">).</li>
</ul></li>
<li><strong>Lines 12–17:</strong> <strong>for</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k%20=%20p"> <strong>to</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?r">
<ul>
<li><strong>Meaning:</strong> This is the main loop. We will look at the slots in the original array <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A"> from index <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?p%20=%202"> to <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?r%20=%205">, and figure out which number goes there by comparing the tops of piles <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L"> and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?R">.</li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<section id="loop-iterations" class="level5">
<h5 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="loop-iterations">Loop Iterations</h5>
<ol type="1">
<li><strong>Loop Iteration 1 (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k%20=%202">):</strong>
<ul>
<li><strong>Compare (Line 13):</strong> Is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L%5B1%5D"> (which is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?4">) <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cle%20R%5B1%5D"> (which is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?2">)? <strong>No.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Action (Lines 16–17):</strong> The right card is smaller. Put <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?R%5B1%5D"> into the main array at <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A%5B2%5D">. Move the right pointer down (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?j%20=%202">).</li>
<li><strong>Array <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A"> is now:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B8,%202,%207,%202,%205,%209%5D"></li>
</ul></li>
<li><strong>Loop Iteration 2 (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k%20=%203">):</strong>
<ul>
<li><strong>Compare (Line 13):</strong> Is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L%5B1%5D"> (which is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?4">) <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cle%20R%5B2%5D"> (which is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?5">)? <strong>Yes.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Action (Lines 14–15):</strong> The left card is smaller. Put <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L%5B1%5D"> into the main array at <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A%5B3%5D">. Move the left pointer down (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?i%20=%202">).</li>
<li><strong>Array <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A"> is now:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B8,%202,%204,%202,%205,%209%5D"></li>
</ul></li>
<li><strong>Loop Iteration 3 (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k%20=%204">):</strong>
<ul>
<li><strong>Compare (Line 13):</strong> Is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L%5B2%5D"> (which is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?7">) <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cle%20R%5B2%5D"> (which is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?5">)? <strong>No.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Action (Lines 16–17):</strong> The right card is smaller. Put <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?R%5B2%5D"> into the main array at <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A%5B4%5D">. Move the right pointer down (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?j%20=%203">).</li>
<li><strong>Array <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A"> is now:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B8,%202,%204,%205,%205,%209%5D"></li>
</ul></li>
<li><strong>Loop Iteration 4 (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k%20=%205">):</strong>
<ul>
<li><strong>Compare (Line 13):</strong> Is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L%5B2%5D"> (which is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?7">) <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cle%20R%5B3%5D"> (which is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cinfty">)? <strong>Yes.</strong> <em>(This is why the sentinel is genius! Any real number is less than <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cinfty">, so it forces the remaining cards in <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L"> to be picked up).</em></li>
<li><strong>Action (Lines 14–15):</strong> The left card is smaller. Put <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L%5B2%5D"> into the main array at <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A%5B5%5D">. Move the left pointer down (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?i%20=%203">).</li>
<li><strong>Array <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A"> is now:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B8,%202,%204,%205,%207,%209%5D"></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
</section>
</section>
<section id="conclusion" class="level4">
<h4 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="conclusion">Conclusion</h4>
<p>The loop finishes because <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?k"> reached <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?r%20=%205">.</p>
<p>Our original array <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?A"> went from <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B8,%204,%207,%202,%205,%209%5D"> to <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B8,%202,%204,%205,%207,%209%5D">.</p>
<p>The target section from indices 2 through 5 is now perfectly merged and sorted!</p>
<hr>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="concrete-example-tracing-merge-sort-1" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="concrete-example-tracing-merge-sort-1">8. Concrete Example: Tracing Merge Sort</h2>
<p>To understand how Merge Sort operates in practice, let us trace the algorithm on an unsorted 8-element array:</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0AA%20=%20%5B5,%202,%204,%207,%201,%203,%202,%206%5D%0A"></p>
<section id="step-1-the-divide-phase" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-1-the-divide-phase">Step 1: The Divide Phase</h3>
<p>The algorithm recursively splits the array in half until every subsequence contains only a single element:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Split 1:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B5,%202,%204,%207%5D"> and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B1,%203,%202,%206%5D"></li>
<li><strong>Split 2:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B5,%202%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B4,%207%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B1,%203%5D">, and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B2,%206%5D"></li>
<li><strong>Base Case (Length 1):</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B5%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B2%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B4%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B7%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B1%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B3%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B2%5D">, and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B6%5D"></li>
</ul>
<p>At this point, the recursion bottoms out because sequences of length 1 are trivially sorted.</p>
</section>
<section id="step-2-the-combine-phase-merging" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-2-the-combine-phase-merging">Step 2: The Combine Phase (Merging)</h3>
<p>The auxiliary procedure <code>MERGE</code> combines the small sorted subarrays back together level-by-level:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Merge to size 2:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B2,%205%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B4,%207%5D">, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B1,%203%5D">, and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B2,%206%5D"></li>
<li><strong>Merge to size 4:</strong> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B2,%204,%205,%207%5D"> and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5B1,%202,%203,%206%5D"></li>
<li><strong>Final Merge to size 8:</strong> We call <code>MERGE</code> on the two halves <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?L%20=%20%5B2,%204,%205,%207%5D"> and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?R%20=%20%5B1,%202,%203,%206%5D">.</li>
</ul>


</section>
</section>

 ]]></description>
